1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,860
Once upon a time, there was a handsome slave.

2
00:00:07,680 --> 00:00:12,980
What bound him were not heavy chains, but the love of a princess.

3
00:00:14,460 --> 00:00:20,660
Every day, every night, the princess whispered her love to the slave,

4
00:00:21,020 --> 00:00:23,820
and the slave responded in kind.

5
00:00:25,220 --> 00:00:28,180
Bound body, bound emotions.

6
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:37,460
The slave or the princess, which of them is really the one who is unable to move?

7
00:02:25,437 --> 00:02:54,617
Let go of me. I can walk by myself.

8
00:02:54,617 --> 00:02:56,617
No!

9
00:02:56,617 --> 00:03:01,617
That's right. Princess Tutu helped me and then…

10
00:03:01,617 --> 00:03:07,617
Binding my wounds. What kind of a useless ch…

11
00:03:07,617 --> 00:03:09,617
Hey.

12
00:03:09,617 --> 00:03:12,617
Oh, Fakir. How are you?

13
00:03:12,617 --> 00:03:15,617
Don't give me that. Why are you still Tutu?

14
00:03:15,617 --> 00:03:22,617
What? Oh, I thought it might be bad if I went in the boys' dorm looking like normal.

15
00:03:22,617 --> 00:03:25,617
Was that weird?

16
00:03:25,617 --> 00:03:28,617
No. Sorry for having troubled you with this.

17
00:03:28,617 --> 00:03:32,617
It was no trouble. Oh, you're able to get up then.

18
00:03:32,617 --> 00:03:35,617
Hey, listen. This doesn't mean I plan on cooperating with you.

19
00:03:35,617 --> 00:03:38,617
But you're going out to look for Muto, aren't you?

20
00:03:38,617 --> 00:03:44,617
We could at least cooperate on that, right? Let's look for Muto together.

21
00:03:44,617 --> 00:04:04,617
You can forget about everything. All you need to fill that void is here in my arms.

22
00:04:04,617 --> 00:04:15,617
No one shall enter here. It shall just be you and me. So I am the only one that you have to give your love to. Now tell me that you love only me.

23
00:04:15,617 --> 00:04:19,617
I love only you, Krehi. Nobody else.

24
00:04:19,617 --> 00:04:20,617
Honestly?

25
00:04:20,617 --> 00:04:21,617
Honestly.

26
00:04:23,617 --> 00:04:26,617
What's that? How much?

27
00:04:30,617 --> 00:04:35,617
If you love me, then smile for me. Don't you remember the festival?

28
00:04:35,617 --> 00:04:36,617
How?

29
00:04:43,617 --> 00:04:48,617
Have you regressed to the doll you used to be? Because I withdrew that piece of your heart?

30
00:04:48,617 --> 00:04:51,617
Have you shut out all your other emotions because of that?

31
00:04:51,617 --> 00:05:00,617
If that's true, then fine. If you're going to love someone else better for you not to love anyone.

32
00:05:01,617 --> 00:05:06,617
It's your fault, you know. You wouldn't so much as look at me when I love you so much.

33
00:05:07,617 --> 00:05:10,617
No. You're not the one to blame.

34
00:05:11,617 --> 00:05:16,617
That's right. If you hadn't begun to regain your heart, everything would have progressed like it should have.

35
00:05:16,617 --> 00:05:21,617
I wouldn't have remembered that I... that I was really a crow.

36
00:05:22,617 --> 00:05:24,617
It's all the fault of that nuisance.

37
00:05:25,617 --> 00:05:26,617
A pest like that.

38
00:05:27,617 --> 00:05:29,617
The sooner we're rid of her, the better for us.

39
00:05:30,617 --> 00:05:33,617
A single prince has no need of two princesses.

40
00:05:34,617 --> 00:05:35,617
Right?

41
00:05:36,617 --> 00:05:37,617
Herr Drosselmeyer?

42
00:05:38,617 --> 00:05:41,617
What? Impossible! Did I just hear her call my name?

43
00:05:41,617 --> 00:05:43,617
You're watching from somewhere, yes?

44
00:05:43,617 --> 00:05:47,617
You have guts to call on me.

45
00:05:48,617 --> 00:05:50,617
Guts enough to offer you the best story ever.

46
00:05:51,617 --> 00:05:52,617
What? Really?

47
00:05:52,617 --> 00:05:55,617
The best of stories demands the best of endings.

48
00:05:56,617 --> 00:05:58,617
And for that, I need a worthy stage.

49
00:05:59,617 --> 00:06:02,617
You're right. And I have a stage I've been saving.

50
00:06:03,617 --> 00:06:06,617
A lake that no one has visited in 200 years.

51
00:06:07,617 --> 00:06:09,617
Do allow me to show you the way.

52
00:06:09,617 --> 00:06:12,617
Mewto! He's not here either.

53
00:06:15,617 --> 00:06:16,617
He's not around.

54
00:06:17,617 --> 00:06:18,617
Of course he is.

55
00:06:18,617 --> 00:06:19,617
It's just that we haven't been able to find him.

56
00:06:19,617 --> 00:06:20,617
Hm?

57
00:06:20,617 --> 00:06:22,617
Oh! The lesson room!

58
00:06:23,617 --> 00:06:24,617
Huh?

59
00:06:24,617 --> 00:06:25,617
He might be dancing there right now, huh?

60
00:06:26,617 --> 00:06:27,617
And why's that?

61
00:06:27,617 --> 00:06:28,617
Huh?

62
00:06:28,617 --> 00:06:29,617
Because Mewto loves to dance, and that's where…

63
00:06:29,617 --> 00:06:30,617
I don't think he is.

64
00:06:30,617 --> 00:06:31,617
He might be dancing there right now, huh?

65
00:06:31,617 --> 00:06:32,617
And why's that?

66
00:06:32,617 --> 00:06:33,617
Huh? Because Mewto loves to dance, and that's where…

67
00:06:33,617 --> 00:06:34,617
I don't think he'll be there.

68
00:06:34,617 --> 00:06:36,617
But, but the last time he was taken, he was back before we knew it, right?

69
00:06:36,617 --> 00:06:37,617
So, I thought it might be the same this time.

70
00:06:37,617 --> 00:06:38,617
Besides, I can't think of anywhere else.

71
00:06:38,617 --> 00:06:39,617
We can check it out. We've nothing to lose.

72
00:06:39,617 --> 00:06:40,617
Huh?

73
00:06:40,617 --> 00:06:41,617
Huh?

74
00:06:41,617 --> 00:06:43,617
Oh, wait for me!

75
00:06:46,617 --> 00:07:03,617
Yeah?

76
00:07:03,617 --> 00:07:06,617
Hey…

77
00:07:06,617 --> 00:07:11,157
The school sure is quiet on Sundays.

78
00:07:11,157 --> 00:07:13,157
I guess.

79
00:07:13,157 --> 00:07:19,157
Is that Miyuto?

80
00:07:19,157 --> 00:07:24,957
Hey, I get to see you.

81
00:07:24,997 --> 00:07:27,517
What? Where? What? What?

82
00:07:27,517 --> 00:07:28,477
Huh?

83
00:07:28,477 --> 00:07:29,397
Huh?

84
00:07:29,397 --> 00:07:32,557
Huh?

85
00:07:32,557 --> 00:07:33,557
Whoa!

86
00:07:33,557 --> 00:07:34,557
Huh?

87
00:07:34,557 --> 00:07:35,557
Huh?

88
00:07:35,557 --> 00:07:36,557
Huh?

89
00:07:36,557 --> 00:07:37,557
Huh?

90
00:07:37,557 --> 00:07:38,557
Huh?

91
00:07:38,557 --> 00:07:39,557
Oh?

92
00:07:39,557 --> 00:07:40,557
I can see you.

93
00:07:40,557 --> 00:07:41,557
Huh?

94
00:07:41,557 --> 00:07:42,557
Huh?

95
00:07:42,557 --> 00:07:43,557
What?

96
00:07:43,557 --> 00:07:44,557
Huh?

97
00:07:44,557 --> 00:07:45,557
Huh?

98
00:07:45,557 --> 00:07:46,557
Huh?

99
00:07:46,557 --> 00:07:47,557
Huh?

100
00:07:47,557 --> 00:07:48,557
Huh?

101
00:07:48,557 --> 00:07:49,057
Huh?

102
00:07:49,057 --> 00:07:49,157
Huh?

103
00:07:49,157 --> 00:07:57,157
Who dares to intrude upon my Sunday practice?

104
00:07:57,157 --> 00:07:59,157
Oh, Miss Duck.

105
00:07:59,157 --> 00:08:03,157
This time I will punish you for disturbing my tireless effort.

106
00:08:03,157 --> 00:08:06,157
I will! Have you marry me right now!

107
00:08:06,157 --> 00:08:08,157
I'm so sorry!

108
00:08:11,157 --> 00:08:13,157
What were you doing?

109
00:08:13,157 --> 00:08:15,157
But... but...

110
00:08:19,157 --> 00:08:23,157
Hello there!

111
00:08:23,157 --> 00:08:25,157
Miuto?

112
00:08:25,157 --> 00:08:30,157
So Miuto's okay! Thank goodness he—

113
00:08:30,157 --> 00:08:33,157
Wait! You know the story of the Prince and the Raven?

114
00:08:33,157 --> 00:08:37,157
It's a tale of a brave prince who battles a monster raven.

115
00:08:37,157 --> 00:08:40,157
There was a knight whom the prince trusted,

116
00:08:40,157 --> 00:08:44,157
but this same knight was torn in two by the claws of the raven.

117
00:08:44,157 --> 00:08:48,157
Without the knight even landing a single blow with his sword,

118
00:08:48,157 --> 00:08:52,157
a useless wretch who could only talk of protection.

119
00:08:54,157 --> 00:08:57,157
That's why the prince suffered such hardship.

120
00:08:57,157 --> 00:08:59,157
The raven had leapt out of the story.

121
00:08:59,157 --> 00:09:03,157
Alone he pursued it, and alone he sealed it away.

122
00:09:03,157 --> 00:09:06,157
Of his own will, he used a forbidden power.

123
00:09:06,157 --> 00:09:07,157
That's right.

124
00:09:07,157 --> 00:09:12,157
The prince drew his sword and took his very own heart out of his body.

125
00:09:12,157 --> 00:09:18,157
What? How? He took it—he took it out himself?

126
00:09:18,157 --> 00:09:19,157
Oh, it's true.

127
00:09:19,157 --> 00:09:21,157
What? True?

128
00:09:21,157 --> 00:09:24,157
You don't know anything, do you, Duck?

129
00:09:24,157 --> 00:09:27,157
What do you know about Princess Tutu?

130
00:09:27,157 --> 00:09:30,157
Princess Tutu? Nothing! I mean, I don't know!

131
00:09:30,157 --> 00:09:35,157
You see, in The Prince and the Raven, Princess Tutu is only presented in a few sentences.

132
00:09:35,157 --> 00:09:40,157
A miserable existence which none of the characters of the story wanted to take on.

133
00:09:40,157 --> 00:09:45,157
An insignificant existence which even the story left by the wayside.

134
00:09:45,157 --> 00:09:48,157
Someone who could never hope to catch the prince's eye.

135
00:09:48,157 --> 00:09:51,157
A little added flourish.

136
00:09:51,157 --> 00:09:52,157
Oh, poor thing.

137
00:09:52,157 --> 00:09:56,157
But Rue, why are you telling me this story now?

138
00:09:57,157 --> 00:09:59,157
So you still haven't figured it out?

139
00:10:00,157 --> 00:10:02,157
Rue doesn't even really exist.

140
00:10:08,157 --> 00:10:09,157
What?

141
00:10:09,157 --> 00:10:13,157
Now then, you have finally figured it out, Princess Tutu.

142
00:10:13,157 --> 00:10:15,157
Princess... Crazy?

143
00:10:15,157 --> 00:10:18,157
No way! You can't be, cause you're my friend!

144
00:10:18,157 --> 00:10:21,157
We used to chat together and dance together and—

145
00:10:21,157 --> 00:10:22,157
Come on, knock it off.

146
00:10:22,157 --> 00:10:23,157
That's true.

147
00:10:23,157 --> 00:10:26,157
But the time has come to put an end to all that foolishness.

148
00:10:27,157 --> 00:10:28,157
Rue, please!

149
00:10:28,157 --> 00:10:33,157
I only came to retrieve something the prince left behind, so I'll take my leave now.

150
00:10:33,157 --> 00:10:34,157
Left behind?

151
00:10:34,157 --> 00:10:38,157
It is not something for a mere failure of a knight to have in his custody.

152
00:10:38,157 --> 00:10:40,157
The prince's sword, but when did she get—

153
00:10:40,157 --> 00:10:42,157
Rue, no!

154
00:10:42,157 --> 00:10:45,157
Hurry up and come rescue the prince!

155
00:10:49,157 --> 00:10:51,157
Oh, Miss Eero!

156
00:10:52,157 --> 00:10:53,157
Miss Eero!

157
00:10:55,157 --> 00:10:57,157
Water is drawn to fire,

158
00:10:57,157 --> 00:10:58,157
Fire to darkness,

159
00:10:58,157 --> 00:11:00,157
Darkness to silence.

160
00:11:00,157 --> 00:11:02,157
Come, let us go.

161
00:11:02,157 --> 00:11:03,157
Go where?

162
00:11:03,157 --> 00:11:05,157
To where you must go.

163
00:11:05,157 --> 00:11:06,157
We must go.

164
00:11:06,157 --> 00:11:07,157
Aw...

165
00:11:07,157 --> 00:11:11,157
This place...

166
00:11:11,157 --> 00:11:12,157
Uh, Miss Eero?

167
00:11:12,157 --> 00:11:13,157
Miss Eero?

168
00:11:27,157 --> 00:11:29,157
It's locked.

169
00:11:29,157 --> 00:11:33,337
This place, uh, Ms. Adol?

170
00:11:37,117 --> 00:11:38,197
It's locked.

171
00:11:42,957 --> 00:11:47,017
You can go to where the Prince and Krehi are from here.

172
00:11:47,397 --> 00:11:48,617
An entrance here?

173
00:11:49,057 --> 00:11:49,857
Go on.

174
00:11:50,577 --> 00:11:53,997
Thanks a lot, Ms. Adol, for always being so kind to me.

175
00:11:54,677 --> 00:11:56,037
This is not kindness.

176
00:11:56,317 --> 00:11:56,517
Huh?

177
00:11:56,517 --> 00:11:59,277
Puppets follow the pull of their strings.

178
00:11:59,717 --> 00:12:00,357
Puppets?

179
00:12:00,897 --> 00:12:02,497
Yes, I am a puppet.

180
00:12:03,337 --> 00:12:06,197
I possess neither feelings nor a heartbeat.

181
00:12:06,577 --> 00:12:11,537
But, Ms. Adol, you've taught me all sorts of things and you've been so friendly.

182
00:12:12,057 --> 00:12:14,697
That's why I think of you like a...

183
00:12:14,697 --> 00:12:18,337
You think of me like that because that was the role I was appointed.

184
00:12:19,317 --> 00:12:21,157
My orders end here.

185
00:12:21,477 --> 00:12:22,877
Now go on, Duck.

186
00:12:23,137 --> 00:12:24,417
Whose orders are that?

187
00:12:24,417 --> 00:12:26,537
Miss Adol?

188
00:12:27,097 --> 00:12:29,217
Now go on, Duck.

189
00:12:30,357 --> 00:12:31,397
Miss Adol?

190
00:12:32,137 --> 00:12:33,357
Thanks a lot.

191
00:12:33,797 --> 00:12:34,677
We'll go now.

192
00:12:36,077 --> 00:12:36,717
Duck.

193
00:12:42,717 --> 00:12:44,537
Such a warm face.

194
00:12:45,077 --> 00:12:46,357
Such soft skin.

195
00:12:47,357 --> 00:12:48,417
Miss Adol, I...

196
00:12:48,417 --> 00:12:50,417
Miss Adol, I...

197
00:12:50,417 --> 00:12:52,597
Now, you must hurry.

198
00:12:54,057 --> 00:12:55,217
Okay, let's go.

199
00:12:59,217 --> 00:13:00,677
Good grief.

200
00:13:00,757 --> 00:13:01,977
You's a puppet too long.

201
00:13:02,057 --> 00:13:05,157
They start getting attached to things other than strings.

202
00:13:05,337 --> 00:13:07,117
Things like people's feelings.

203
00:13:08,137 --> 00:13:13,277
Don't you forget, your role is to add a glow to the story in my place.

204
00:13:13,277 --> 00:13:15,897
That's about all you're capable of doing anyhow.

205
00:13:16,237 --> 00:13:19,477
Not knowing your place in the world is dangerous, you know.

206
00:13:19,477 --> 00:13:20,797
Scary.

207
00:13:36,277 --> 00:13:36,797
Scary!

208
00:13:37,377 --> 00:13:37,797
Ow!

209
00:13:38,517 --> 00:13:40,077
Idiot, walk towards the middle.

210
00:13:40,217 --> 00:13:42,177
You're already careless enough as it is.

211
00:13:42,817 --> 00:13:43,417
Huh?

212
00:13:43,417 --> 00:13:51,097
Wow, this place is kind of incredible.

213
00:13:51,297 --> 00:13:51,477
Oh!

214
00:13:53,097 --> 00:13:54,837
Okay, okay, eyes forward.

215
00:13:55,177 --> 00:13:55,357
Oh!

216
00:13:56,397 --> 00:13:56,837
Whoa!

217
00:14:00,597 --> 00:14:03,277
Um, you really are Princess Tutu, aren't you?

218
00:14:03,737 --> 00:14:04,157
Huh?

219
00:14:05,157 --> 00:14:06,437
Yeah, what of it?

220
00:14:06,457 --> 00:14:09,797
I thought Princess Tutu was more, uh, you know.

221
00:14:10,157 --> 00:14:10,537
Huh?

222
00:14:10,537 --> 00:14:11,257
Never mind.

223
00:14:14,017 --> 00:14:15,217
Say, Fakir.

224
00:14:15,357 --> 00:14:16,097
What is it?

225
00:14:16,877 --> 00:14:18,717
N-nothing, never mind.

226
00:14:19,177 --> 00:14:19,897
What the heck?

227
00:14:20,097 --> 00:14:22,377
If you didn't want to say, just keep your mouth shut.

228
00:14:22,577 --> 00:14:24,657
Oh, no, it's not like that.

229
00:14:24,777 --> 00:14:28,857
But just so you know, I don't think you're no good as a knight or anything.

230
00:14:29,437 --> 00:14:30,657
What are you getting at?

231
00:14:31,097 --> 00:14:32,917
I'm not really trying to get at anything.

232
00:14:33,617 --> 00:14:36,897
It's just, I didn't think you were very nice when we first met.

233
00:14:37,237 --> 00:14:39,237
But now I feel like I know you a little better.

234
00:14:39,237 --> 00:14:40,357
I'll say this right now.

235
00:14:40,677 --> 00:14:42,997
I have no intention of cooperating with you.

236
00:14:43,257 --> 00:14:44,957
I'll help Mewtwo in my own way.

237
00:14:45,217 --> 00:14:45,937
End of story.

238
00:14:46,597 --> 00:14:46,957
Hmm.

239
00:14:47,977 --> 00:14:49,117
I know that.

240
00:14:53,497 --> 00:14:54,537
Wow, you know?

241
00:14:55,977 --> 00:14:56,337
Hmm?

242
00:14:57,497 --> 00:14:59,017
Never mind, it's nothing.

243
00:14:59,437 --> 00:15:00,337
What is your problem?

244
00:15:00,477 --> 00:15:02,377
Quit stopping in the middle of your sentences.

245
00:15:02,377 --> 00:15:09,857
Well, the truth is that I never thought about things like, what do I like about Mewtwo?

246
00:15:11,597 --> 00:15:11,877
Oh.

247
00:15:11,877 --> 00:15:19,277
The first time I saw Mewtwo, it was mostly me just thinking he was handsome.

248
00:15:19,877 --> 00:15:22,757
But when I looked closer, his eyes looked so lonely.

249
00:15:23,077 --> 00:15:27,657
And I thought if I became Princess Tutu, then maybe I could do something for him.

250
00:15:29,177 --> 00:15:33,097
At the start, that's all there really was to it.

251
00:15:33,097 --> 00:15:36,477
But now, I...

252
00:15:36,477 --> 00:15:42,377
Damn it!

253
00:15:42,377 --> 00:15:44,457
Fuck him!

254
00:15:44,477 --> 00:15:44,777
Run!

255
00:15:48,997 --> 00:15:49,637
Fuck!

256
00:15:51,097 --> 00:15:52,057
Come on!

257
00:15:52,217 --> 00:15:52,777
Idiot!

258
00:15:52,777 --> 00:16:07,777
Sorry, are you hurt at all?

259
00:16:08,777 --> 00:16:10,237
It's a miracle I'm not.

260
00:16:11,597 --> 00:16:12,757
What is this place?

261
00:16:15,757 --> 00:16:18,057
I guess we'll just have to climb back up.

262
00:16:19,057 --> 00:16:19,937
Uh...

263
00:16:19,937 --> 00:16:20,777
Oh!

264
00:16:20,777 --> 00:16:23,897
We might be able to get out through the water.

265
00:16:25,297 --> 00:16:29,277
I could go check it out if I became a bird, but...

266
00:16:29,277 --> 00:16:30,597
It's covered in moss.

267
00:16:30,697 --> 00:16:31,857
I doubt we can climb it.

268
00:16:31,937 --> 00:16:32,497
Damn!

269
00:16:33,957 --> 00:16:35,617
Since it's Vakir...

270
00:16:36,837 --> 00:16:37,677
Vakir?

271
00:16:38,757 --> 00:16:39,657
What is it?

272
